                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array {
                      \&amp; c          &amp; \leftarrow    &amp; r &amp; \rightarrow &amp; d &amp;  \\
                      Id_c &amp; \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow &amp; \chi_r \\
                      \&amp; c          &amp; \leftarrow      &amp; \in_c      &amp; \rightarrow       &amp; \Omega^c &amp; \\
                      }
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                may lack some pullbacks, then we simply require that the pullback that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                is to equal must exist. But arguably we should require, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^c
                is to be a power object, that this pullback exists for any given map
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
